---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Terms and Conditions — Free Online Exam Timer | FreeExamTimer"
  description="Terms and conditions for using FreeExamTimer. Free educational license, invigilator operational guidelines, backup clock recommendations, and acceptable use policy."
  canonicalUrl="https://freeexamtimer.com/terms"
>
  <Nav active="terms" />

  <main class="mx-auto max-w-[800px] px-5 pt-24 pb-20">
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="mb-10">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal & Compliance</p>
      <h1 class="mt-2 text-[36px] md:text-[44px] leading-[44px] font-semibold tracking-[-2px]">
        Terms and Conditions
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--text-secondary)]">
        Please read these terms carefully before utilizing FreeExamTimer in formal examinations, classrooms, or mock testing environments.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 text-xs text-[var(--text-muted)] font-mono">
        <span class="rounded bg-[var(--border-color)] px-2 py-1">Last Updated: January 2026</span>
        <span class="rounded bg-[var(--border-color)] px-2 py-1">Terms Version: 2.1</span>
        <span class="rounded bg-blue-500/10 text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 px-2 py-1 font-medium">Free Educational License</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Essential Notice Card for Invigilators -->
    <div class="card p-6 mb-12 bg-[var(--bg-elevated)] border-l-4 border-l-amber-500">
      <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
        <svg class="h-5 w-5 text-amber-500 shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 9v2m0 4h.01m-6.938 4h13.856c1.54 0 2.502-1.667 1.732-3L13.732 4c-.77-1.333-2.694-1.333-3.464 0L3.34 16c-.77 1.333.192 3 1.732 3z"/>
        </svg>
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">Crucial Exam Hall Advisory</h2>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">
            FreeExamTimer is an auxiliary visual clock designed to assist teachers and invigilators. As mandated by standard examination codes worldwide (e.g., JCQ regulations in the UK), <strong>invigilators must always maintain an official secondary clock (such as a battery wall clock) in the examination room</strong>. Ensure projection laptops are connected to AC mains power.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Terms Sections -->
    <article class="space-y-10 text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] tracking-tight">
          1. Agreement to Terms
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6">
          By accessing or using FreeExamTimer (freeexamtimer.com), you confirm that you have read, understood, and agreed to be bound by these Terms and Conditions. If you do not agree, please discontinue using the service.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] tracking-tight">
          2. Educational License & Permitted Use
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6">
          FreeExamTimer is granted to you free of charge under a non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable license for educational, instructional, commercial, and personal exam timing. You may freely project the timer in:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-sm pl-5 list-disc">
          <li>Public, private, and charter primary and secondary schools</li>
          <li>Colleges, universities, and polytechnics</li>
          <li>Commercial test centers, tutoring companies, and academic bootcamps</li>
          <li>Home study and self-timed mock testing</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] tracking-tight">
          3. Hardware, Battery & System Sleep Guidelines
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6">
          While FreeExamTimer implements the modern W3C Screen Wake Lock API to prevent host operating systems from entering sleep mode, hardware behavior may vary depending on operating system policies, battery-saver profiles, and corporate IT group policies.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6">
          You agree that you are solely responsible for ensuring your hardware remains powered, unmuted (if audible chimes are required), and configured to avoid unexpected automatic restarts or power-saving screen cutoffs during an active test.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] tracking-tight">
          4. Intellectual Property
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6">
          The FreeExamTimer brand, bespoke audio synthesis algorithms, visual layouts, icons, typography integration, and digital assets are protected by applicable intellectual property laws. You may not sell, sub-license, repackage, or distribute modified copies of FreeExamTimer without express written authorization.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] tracking-tight">
          5. Acceptable Use
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6">
          You agree not to engage in any activity that interferes with or disrupts the application, including:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-sm pl-5 list-disc">
          <li>Attempting denial-of-service (DDoS) attacks against the hosting network.</li>
          <li>De-compiling or reverse engineering proprietary assets.</li>
          <li>Framing the website within third-party advertising-heavy frames without attribution.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] tracking-tight">
          6. Disclaimer of Warranties
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6">
          FreeExamTimer is provided on an <strong class="text-[var(--text-primary)]">"as is" and "as available"</strong> basis without warranties of any kind, whether express or implied. We do not warrant that the website will be uninterrupted, error-free, or entirely compatible with all historical web browsers or non-standard projection hardware.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] tracking-tight">
          7. Limitation of Liability
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6">
          In no event shall the creators or maintainers of FreeExamTimer be liable for any direct, indirect, incidental, or consequential damages resulting from the use or inability to use the timer. This includes, without limitation, candidate examination scores, missed paper submissions, examination cancellations, or disputes between examination centers and candidates.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] tracking-tight">
          8. Governing Law & Modifications
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6">
          We reserve the right to revise these Terms and Conditions at our discretion. Continuing to access FreeExamTimer after modifications constitutes your acceptance of the updated terms.
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>

    <!-- Bottom Actions -->
    <div class="card mt-12 p-6 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-start sm:items-center justify-between gap-4">
      <div>
        <p class="font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)]">Need official clarification for your exam board?</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-[var(--text-secondary)]">
          Contact our support team for compliance queries.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 shrink-0">
        <a href="/contact" class="btn-app">Contact us</a>
        <a href="/" class="btn-pill">Open timer</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
